<title>GERMANY: German banks welcome Finnish marrka's ERM link.</title>
<headline>German banks welcome Finnish marrka's ERM link.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>An association of German banks on Monday welcomed the Finnish markka's entry to the European Rate Mechanism at the weekend, praising Finland's low inflation rates and budgetary controls.</p>
<p>&quot;Moreover the markka's fluctuation with the mark has been in a tight range for the past two years. The European Rate Mechanism will be strengthened as an area of currency stability by Finland's entry,&quot; the BdB banking association said.</p>
<p>The acceptance of Finland also indicated that European Union members were serious about achieving economic and monetary union, the BdB said in a statement.</p>
</text>
